{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02346",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 3.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.93,
      "end_seconds": 8.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Okay, so afternoon, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.28,
      "end_seconds": 13.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.55,
      "end_seconds": 27.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.03,
      "text": "It's attacks of spinning lasting hours. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.47,
      "end_seconds": 31.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.16,
      "end_seconds": 41.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Okay, so I'd say about three months. Actually, no, closer to about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.14,
      "end_seconds": 46.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.25,
      "end_seconds": 55.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Okay, um, so I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.82,
      "end_seconds": 59.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.04,
      "end_seconds": 81.31,
      "duration_seconds": 21.27,
      "text": "Hearing getting worse goes along with it, um, most of the time. Uh, the hearing getting worse? That's been for one week. Okay, uh, so I've had a full feeling in the ear too, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.31,
      "end_seconds": 86.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.73,
      "end_seconds": 89.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.54,
      "end_seconds": 98.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.79,
      "end_seconds": 116.62,
      "duration_seconds": 15.83,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for two years. Uh, I have diabetes, for about ten years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.5,
      "end_seconds": 126.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure and diabetes, that matches what I have here. Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.28,
      "end_seconds": 131.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Well, no allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.69,
      "end_seconds": 135.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.74,
      "end_seconds": 149.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.16,
      "end_seconds": 159.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.1,
      "end_seconds": 174.88,
      "duration_seconds": 14.78,
      "text": "Amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day. Gliclazide. I take it 80 milligrams, twice a day. Let me think, before this I was on metoprolol; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.63,
      "end_seconds": 180.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "A few quick ones: ear discharge or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.38,
      "end_seconds": 185.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Yeah, no, no ear discharge or headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.57,
      "end_seconds": 189.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Any weakness or double vision at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.63,
      "end_seconds": 195.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.3,
      "end_seconds": 199.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.61,
      "end_seconds": 205.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Okay, so no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.05,
      "end_seconds": 209.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.9,
      "end_seconds": 213.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Nothing there, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.04,
      "end_seconds": 223.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.46,
      "end_seconds": 237.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.49,
      "end_seconds": 251.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 113 over 73, heart rate 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.29,
      "end_seconds": 256.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Well, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.76,
      "end_seconds": 260.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.7,
      "end_seconds": 265.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.96,
      "end_seconds": 268.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.68,
      "end_seconds": 291.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "The ear drums look normal and the hearing is reduced on the left."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.87,
      "end_seconds": 294.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.53,
      "end_seconds": 313.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.85,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Having listened and examined, it points towards Meniere's disease. I'm prescribing betahistine, 16 milligrams, three times a day, long term. That's for vertigo. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.22,
      "end_seconds": 317.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.54,
      "end_seconds": 320.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
